# Accepted text-check findings. One entry per line:
#   rule | file pattern | word (optional) | reason
# The rule is required and cannot be *. tools/text_check.py has the rules.

# The design document names game parts and actions with -ing words
# (Breeding pod, heating towers, Packing). Renaming them would change the
# design.
ing-form | docs/design.md | | names of game parts and actions in the design
ing-form | docs/superpowers/specs/*-lifecycle-design.md | | names of game parts and research (Breeding pod, Sulfur processing)

# The review reports record what reviewers said and quote the old spec,
# including its American spellings.
spelling | docs/superpowers/reviews/*.md | color | quotes the old spec
spelling | docs/superpowers/reviews/*.md | behavior | quotes the old spec
ing-form | docs/superpowers/reviews/*.md | | records the reviewers' wording
passive | docs/superpowers/reviews/*.md | | records the reviewers' wording
perfect-tense | docs/superpowers/reviews/*.md | | records the reviewers' wording
sentence-length | docs/superpowers/reviews/*.md | | records the reviewers' wording
word | docs/superpowers/reviews/*.md | | records the reviewers' wording
paragraph-length | docs/superpowers/reviews/*.md | | records the reviewers' wording
modal-passive | docs/superpowers/reviews/*.md | | records the reviewers' wording

# The plan follows the writing-plans format ("Modify:" in file lists) and
# the functional-core work loop, which defines "attempt".
word | docs/superpowers/plans/*.md | modify | the writing-plans file-list format
word | docs/superpowers/plans/*.md | attempt | a term the work loop defines
word | docs/superpowers/plans/*.md | utilize | the planted mistake for the checker test
